					Il.
					22.60
				</span></i>
			, al., <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				116
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Mimn.
				2.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				8.71
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γήρως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					174
				</span></i>
			, 
				Att.
			 (v. infr.): dat. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γήραϊ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					7.99
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.24
			</span></i>, 
				contr.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γήρᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					507
				</span></i>
			, etc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γήρατι</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Adam.
				<u>Phgn.</u>
				1.14
			</span></i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆρος</span>):—<i>old age</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ. λυγρόν</span>”
